; the exact measurement annotated on an engineering drawing.
; a dimension is not a description — it is a specification.
; it says: this distance MUST be this value (within tolerance).
; 
; types of dimensions:
; linear:      distance between two points, lines, or surfaces.
; angular:     angle between two lines or surfaces. degrees or radians.
; radial:      radius of an arc or circle. prefix R. e.g. R25.
; diametric:   diameter of a circle. prefix ∅. e.g. ∅50.
; arc length:  length along a curve.
; 
; dimension line: thin line with arrowheads showing extent of measurement.
; extension line: thin line from the feature to the dimension line.
; leader line: diagonal line with arrowhead pointing to a feature, note at end.
; 
; units: mm in most countries (ISO). inches in USA.
; scale: 1:1 (full size), 1:2 (half), 1:10, 2:1 (enlarged). always stated.
; 
; datum: the reference point or surface from which dimensions are measured.
; all dimensions chain back to the datum — removes accumulated error.
; functional datum: the surface that actually contacts the mating part.
; 
; redundant dimensions: dimensions that can be calculated from others.
; should not appear (creates contradiction if not perfectly consistent).

(kosha dimension
  (vishesa drawing-varga engineering-varga)
  (swarupa subanta measurement)
  (yukta linear angular radial tolerance datum matra))
